### modules/map/components/DeviceMarker.tsx

Custom Leaflet marker for each couple on the map:

```typescript
interface DeviceMarkerProps {
  point: MapDataPoint
  isSelected: boolean
  onClick: () => void
}
```

- Uses Leaflet `DivIcon` for a custom HTML marker (not default pin)
- Marker is a colored circle with glow:
  ```html
  <div style="
    width: 16px;
    height: 16px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: ${statusColor};
    box-shadow: 0 0 8px ${statusColor}, 0 0 16px ${statusColor}40;
    border: 2px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.3);
  "></div>
  ```
- Status colors: Working `#5F8F6B`, Not Working `#B68A3C`, Faulty `#9B3E3E`
- Selected state: white ring (`#F2F2F2`) and larger glow
- Has RF indicator: smaller dot above/beside the main circle (optional visual)
- Tooltip on hover: couple name (use Leaflet `Tooltip`)
- Click: calls `onClick` which triggers popup and trail loading
- Uses React-Leaflet `Marker` component with `icon` prop set to a `DivIcon`

**Creating the DivIcon:**
```typescript
import L from 'leaflet'

const icon = L.divIcon({
  className: '', // clear default leaflet class
  html: `<div style="..."></div>`,
  iconSize: [16, 16],
  iconAnchor: [8, 8],
})
```

